# Development guidelines — __NAME__

This is a generated dPLaaX policy-verifier instance. Refer to the upstream
sources of truth before touching the wiring:

- **dPLaaX auth contract** (grant rules, L1 boundaries):
  <https://github.com/dplaax/spec> (`rules/`); the 3-layer model and the
  ChainPeerService L2-only rule:
  <https://github.com/provin-line/oss/blob/main/docs/protocol/auth.md>
- **`@o3co/auth.policy-verifier.server`** runtime docs: <https://github.com/o3co/auth.policy-verifier>
- **`@provin-line/policy-verifier-dplaax-module`** attribute + rule collectors:
  <https://github.com/provin-line/auth/tree/develop/packages/policy-verifier-dplaax-module>

## Where to add things

| Concern | File |
| --- | --- |
| Per-deployment rule entries | `config/application.conf` `rule.collectors[*].rules` |
| Per-environment overrides | `config/{development,production}.conf` |
| Project-specific `RuleCollector` classes | `src/rules/` + register in `src/main.mts` modules |
| Project-specific `AttributeCollector` classes | `src/collectors/` + same wiring |

## Tests

```bash
__PACKAGE_MANAGER_BIN__ run test
```

The default `src/__tests__/config/configFiles.test.mts` enforces the
ChainPeerService L2-only rule (see dPLaaX auth spec § 2). Extend it as
your deployment's L1 boundary grows.

## Regenerating

To pick up newer dPLaaX or o3co framework pins, re-run
`@provin-line/create-policy-verifier` at the newer release tag and diff the
output against this directory. Hand-edits to deployment payload
(`config/`, `src/rules/`, `src/collectors/`) survive a regenerate when
re-applied; framework wiring (`src/main.mts`, `package.json` deps,
`tsconfig.json`) is overwritten.
